WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.363
- What are the top three
keys to being happy?

00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:14.115
(upbeat sunny music)

00:00:14.351 --> 00:00:17.986
- My name is H-A-N-K, and that spells Hank

00:00:17.986 --> 00:00:19.819
and I am 4 and a half.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.050
- I'm looking for tips
on how to be more happy.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.360
Do you have any advice?

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.140
- If I do something like cool

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.403
it makes me feel like happy.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.530
- I think being with people you love

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.140
will trigger happiness so much

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.040
because you're always
just chillin', you know?

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.140
You chillin'?
- Yeah!

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.930
- When I hang out with my family.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.290
When cats appear.
- Like out of the darkness?

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.341
When they just appear?

00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:46.617
- I wouldn't say like that, but--

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.350
- Oh, okay. (laughing)

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.780
- What can I do to be happier?

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.320
- What stuff you love to do?

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.333
- I love dancing, I love going out to eat,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.860
I love finessing billionaires.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:00.693
- Everyday.
- Okay.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.590
- Even if you're here, for two minutes

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.820
you go outside and you say,
"Guys, I need my two minutes."

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.340
Everyday, and you're gonna go

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.240
and you're gonna turn your favorite jam on

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.843
and you're gonna dance.
- I'm gonna dance?

00:01:09.843 --> 00:01:11.787
- You're doing dance.
- I'm gonna dance.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:12.767
(techno music)

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:15.100
- Get 'em!
- Hey, okay, okay.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.518
- I can't really help you
with finessing billionaires,

00:01:18.518 --> 00:01:19.500
I wish I could.
- You know what?

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.400
I'm still working on that.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.233
- You'll get there, you'll there.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:23.283
- I'll get there.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.983
- What does happiness mean?

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:29.290
- It means feeling, having a good day

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.603
and feeling good about yourself.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.250
- Yeah, that's a good answer.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.623
- I just feel like I could
just slide over a rainbow.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.043
- What are your top
three keys to happiness?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.735
- Cats, chocolate and candy.

00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:45.280
- Oh my gosh.
- And my friends.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.963
And my family.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.826
- I like where your friends
and family come on that list.

00:01:49.826 --> 00:01:50.659
(laughing)

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:52.270
- What's something you do when you want

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.463
to make yourself happy?

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.610
That's a good thing not to do.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.763
- Is it okay to do bad
things if it makes you happy?

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.000
- Depends what kind of bad things, okay?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.000
If you're robbing people's houses

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.480
and that's what makes you
happy, you need to stop.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.930
- Do you ever have a sad day?

00:02:09.029 --> 00:02:09.862
- Well.

00:02:10.904 --> 00:02:14.733
Not really, I usually have happy days.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.593
- That must be so nice.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.420
- Well if you just join the beautiful day

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.533
you'll have a good time.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.142
- Do you have any tips for
making my mornings happier

00:02:24.142 --> 00:02:25.470
so that I get out of bed?

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.740
- If you have an alarm
clock, don't make it

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.550
like that annoying ringing,
make it a pleasant sound

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.310
that makes you really want to get up.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.300
If you love dancing, put dance music

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.670
so it makes you feel
energized and you just dance.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.770
- Oh my gosh.
- Your heart out.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.374
- Like a trap music alarm clock?

00:02:41.374 --> 00:02:42.993
- Yeah.
- That sounds amazing.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.580
- Have you ever heard of depression?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.290
- Yeah, it's a very deep sadness.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.240
It's when something's happened
that you can't recover from

00:02:50.332 --> 00:02:53.210
and you get in this
place where it's so hard

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.103
to come back up.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.510
I've dealt with depression, too.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.460
There have been times where
I went to school everyday

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.300
and just got mauled and bullied

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.710
and it sucked so bad but
I found the people I love

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.603
and the things I love to support me.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.060
You got through it and I got through it

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.860
so tell all the people
who are watching this.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:08.800
- You can get through it.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.653
- My sister hasn't been
talking to me lately.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.733
How do I get her to talk
to me? What can I do?

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.490
- Oh so if I say it louder,
that'll get through to her?

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.453
- Yeah.

00:03:22.453 --> 00:03:24.483
- So sometimes, do you
know what Instagram is?

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.643
- No.

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:29.220
- Okay, I go on my phone
and I can look at pictures

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.740
of what all my friends are doing.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.391
So they're on like vacation,
doing these amazing things

00:03:33.391 --> 00:03:36.232
with their career and
they seem really happy

00:03:36.232 --> 00:03:38.670
and then sometimes that makes me sad

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.080
like I should be doing more.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.960
Do you know any way that
I could not feel that way?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.943
- Maybe if you just not look at them?

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.895
(triumphant music)

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:48.753
- Genius.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.780
You know what, I'm going to
delete my Instagram right now.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.787
I'm just kidding, I can't do that.

00:03:52.787 --> 00:03:54.873
- God.
- What makes you happy?

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.540
- I would say my family
and then my friends.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.820
And I really, really
like going to the beach.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.219
- Me, too, definitely.
- That's a happy place,

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:02.180
let's be honest.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.060
This is good.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.863
- Joyce, what makes you happy?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.120
- I like to collect like
old books so I like to go

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.063
to the library sometimes.
- Awesome.

00:04:08.063 --> 00:04:11.656
- And I like to read really
old dusty romance books

00:04:11.656 --> 00:04:14.990
on weekends because of many reasons

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:16.643
but that's what makes me happy.

00:04:16.643 --> 00:04:17.493
- That's awesome.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.060
- What would you do if there
was something you could do

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.453
to make every person in the world happy?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.420
What do you think that would be?

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.269
Yeah, loving everybody?

00:04:27.269 --> 00:04:29.193
- Yes.
- That's a good answer.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.953
- What do you like to
do with your friends?

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.973
- I like to usually play around with them.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.915
- Like play like dress up?

00:04:36.915 --> 00:04:39.993
- Well we don't really
usually play dress up.

00:04:40.226 --> 00:04:43.023
- Hmm.
- It's been a long time.

00:04:43.143 --> 00:04:44.053
- Same.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.853
- Even if you're feeling
really, really sad, just smile.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.912
Work on your smiling and that will always

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:53.590
make you feel better even
if you're the saddest

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.240
of saddest of sads.
- I like that.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.953
- Just smile.
- Can you give me smile?

00:04:59.314 --> 00:05:00.740
(triangle chiming)

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.723
- If you just don't
think about the badness,

00:05:02.723 --> 00:05:04.633
you'll just have goodness.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.280
- That's really insightful.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.770
- So any last advice for me, Mr. Toby?

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.960
- You are definitely a joyful person.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.800
Your parents named you Joyce for a reason.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:13.910
- Oh good.
- So you should live

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.673
like your name, you should
be Joyce the joyful.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.023
- Thank you so much, Toby.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:21.610
(upbeat music)

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.750
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new channel.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.583
And now your part.

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:33.640
- [Both] Subscribe here.
- That was my part.

